# LF in the working tree on every platform, including Windows.
#
# This is not cosmetic. Test expectations are multi-line raw string literals, so their line
# endings are whatever the .cs file holds on disk - and the CI Windows runner sets
# core.autocrlf=true, which checked those literals out as CRLF while TestFormatter normalized
# the actual output to LF. 38 tests failed on a difference that exists nowhere in the code.
#
# The fixture suite has the same exposure from the other direction: it compares formatter
# output against committed baselines and Sample/ inputs.
#
# Nothing here is renormalized - every file is already stored as LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
